            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bkuntz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so easy and so tasty! I actually didn't have enough time to do it in a slow cooker, so I put everything in a dutch oven and cooked at 400 for about 30 minutes (til the meat thermometer registered 145 degrees). The whole family enjoyed it!\n\nThis afternoon, I took some of the leftovers, added chicken broth and a spoonful of brown sugar and voila! a delicious warming soup!",
            "datePublished": "2008-12-17T13:55:42.390Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HRCHRC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The pork did turn out well, nice and tender. However the sauerkraut was too strong and overpowered everything else. I did make sure to drain the sauerkraut before adding to the slow cooker, but it probably would be good to also rinse it. Additionally, Bavarian sauerkraut (milder, sweeter, and has caraway seeds) would be better than plain/regular sauerkraut.",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-28T03:34:48.837Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeremiah"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent dish for the New Years tradition. No peach flavored tea so used some Craisins. Also added some thyme to flavor the pork. Had to go out to store to get apples so added after first 2 hours of cooking and cooked to perfection. The juices of apple and craisins really added some great taste.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-01T14:41:40.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tom McCullough Sr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved the sauerkraut this way! The pork turned out slightly overcooked but it was because our slow cooker seems to get too hot on high. We will definitely do it again but will cut back to low after three hours. With leftovers, we made South Philly Italian style pork sandwiches with broccoli rabe, provolone, and long hots. Outstanding!",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-07T16:39:14.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cookin Up A Storm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a good one. I did skip the tea and instead subbed in a tablespoon or two of peach jam. I thought the tea would have been just too much liquid but the peach, apple, onion add a nice complexity to the sauerkraut. This is a keeper.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-15T15:58:10.197Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bighairtexan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Oh wow this is so incredibly easy and delicious. My picky eater boyfriend also just LOVED it. I cut the onions up in a \"large dice\", more like chunks, and cut the apples in slices. I forgot to peel them and they were wonderful even with the peel. I used Diet Snapple Peach Tea. Really delish.",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-01T18:13:31.463Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lilcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So simple and so good! I will be putting this in the menu rotation as we love pork chops and this is a yummy way to fix them. I was not able to to find peach ice tea so I used a mango/orange drink. It was good, but would be better with the tea. Next time I will brew some as I have peach tea.",
            "datePublished": "2013-08-29T08:45:42.777Z"
          },
